  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ECONOMIC EMPOWERMENT OF VULNERABLE WOMEN (WOMEN AT RISK OF, AND WOMEN SURVIVORS OF GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE) THROUGH TARGETED SKILLS DEVELOPMENT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to improve the human rights and gender equality of women/girls, especially members of vulnerable groups in BiH, with a specific focus on rural areas in Herzegovina. Women with no education are the most at risk from poverty and represent 41.8 % of all poor women. To address the economic disadvantages of women, the project will prioritise economic empowerment, through training on business planning. The project also aims to raise awareness among women about different types of gender-based violence, and equip potential victims with the knowledge and tools to recognize GBV and seek help.</narrative>
  </description>
